# `mirl compile <file> [-o <path>] [--emit <kind>]`: compile the text for a
# target through mirl.target.compile and write one kind of what the
# compilation makes
#
# a kind is a row of KINDS, a stopping point as mach's --emit names it: the
# module after the pass schedule, the machine form text of the laid out
# functions, masc's listing of the object, the object in the format of the
# target's system, through mink, the default, or the final image the target
# loads as it is, which mink's link makes of the object. the command reads the
# line and reports, and the compilation is the library's.

